{"id": "EUVD-2026-96564", "enisaUuid": "7ca0905e-2f59-3300-8177-5432b3240dc4", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows low-privileged authenticated users to modify message push records by calling PUT /sys/message/sysMessage/edit. Attackers can submit a request body naming any sys_sms record id to overwrite its title, content, receiver address and send status without ownership checks.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:02:01", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_c092_sysmessage_edit.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/message/controller/SysMessageController.java#L79-L84", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sysmessage-edit-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108625", "GHSA-f2px-hmhw-mj87"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6e54557c-7663-3efc-a5a6-2ee89403f95c", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8053e781-ca33-317a-b025-e3050940f13f", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}